  /* ---------------------------------------------------------
     3) FLOATING WISHLIST BUTTON — HIDDEN, TRIGGERED FROM HEADER
     INSTEAD (25th Aug 2026)
     Injected by the "Notify Me!" app (class:
     .nm-wishlist-open-list-button).

     EARLIER APPROACH ABANDONED: trying to visually reposition
     this exact element into the header (via CSS position:fixed,
     even with MutationObservers and a setInterval backstop)
     turned out to be unwinnable — the app continuously replaces
     its own inline style attribute (confirmed via direct
     inspection), fighting any external override faster than a
     safe, non-flickering interval could counter.

     CURRENT APPROACH: a real, native, non-app-controlled icon
     was added directly to the header instead — replacing the old
     Store icon (see snippets/store-locator.liquid) — which, when
     clicked, calls .click() on THIS button, so the app's own real
     wishlist-opening logic still runs. This button itself is
     simply hidden everywhere; it no longer needs to be visible on
     its own, since the header icon is its new, stable trigger
     point. Hiding a display:none element via a stylesheet rule is
     not something the app fights (it only fights position/inset
     properties, not display), so this is fully stable.
     --------------------------------------------------------- */
  .nm-wishlist-open-list-button {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------
     4) INLINE "ADD TO WISHLIST" BUTTON
     Injected by the "Notify Me!" app (class: .nm-wishlist-button
     .nm-PRODUCT_PAGE-wishlist-button). This element is NEVER
     moved in the DOM — it stays exactly where the app originally
     placed it (inside .pdp-action-wrapper), on BOTH mobile and
     desktop. This is deliberate: physically moving the node
     broke its click handling (the app's event delegation is tied
     to its original position in the DOM tree), so instead we only
     change how it's PAINTED on screen via CSS, never its actual
     location — preserving the exact same working behaviour as
     mobile already has.

     Desktop (≥769px): rendered as a small fixed-position icon
     beside the product title. The exact top/left coordinates are
     calculated in snippets/estimated-dispatch.liquid via
     getBoundingClientRect() on the title, then applied as an
     inline style. position:fixed automatically removes it from
     .pdp-action-wrapper's flex layout, so it reserves zero space
     near Buy It Now without needing a separate display:none rule.

     Mobile (≤768px): completely unchanged — identical to the
     compact square that was already working before this update.
     --------------------------------------------------------- */
  @media screen and (min-width: 769px) {
